## Two deviations from the ticket's file list, both deliberate

1. **No `router_audit.tscn`.** The ticket's write allowlist pairs
   `router_audit.gd` with a `.tscn`. Every audit in this port that is invoked as
   `--script res://…` is a `SceneTree` script (`godot/tests/input/reachability_audit.gd`,
   `godot/tests/audits/*`), and a `SceneTree` script cannot be attached to a node in a
   scene — the scene would fail to load, which is worse than not shipping one. No
   scene file was invented for it; the acceptance command is the `--script` form the
   ticket itself specifies.
2. **No `.uid` sidecars yet.** `.uid` files are generated by an editor/import scan,
   not by a headless `--script` run (none appeared: `find godot/src/ui godot/tests/ui
   -name "*.uid"` is empty). The import scan also writes `.import` sidecars into
   `godot/assets/ui/**`, which UIR-01 owns this wave, so this ticket did not run it
   rather than write into another ticket's area. The engine loads both scenes and all
   scripts without the sidecars, as the runs above show; the first import pass that
   runs generates them.

## Interface handed to the next tickets (frozen from here)

```
ScreenRouter (extends Control, mounts its own ScreenHost Control child)
  static ids() -> Array                    the thirteen router ids, document order
  static row(id) / has_id(id)
  static dom_id_of(id) / id_of_dom(dom)    the only bridge between `menu` and `screen-menu`
  static back_target_of(id) -> String      "" for menu/game/result
  static to_actions_of(id) -> Array
  register(id, scene) -> bool              refuses an id outside the table, a null scene
  registered_ids() -> Array
  go_to(id, payload = {}) -> bool          refuses an unknown id (warns, stays)
  active_id() / active_screen() / screen_count() / screen_host()
  signal screen_changed(from_id, to_id)
ScreenContract (extends Control)             base class for every screen
  screen_id() / back_target() / enter(payload) / exit()
  capture_states() -> Array[String]          ["default"] by default
  apply_capture_state(state_id) -> bool      false by default
ScreenShell                                  setup(id) / set_title(id) / set_subtitle(id)
  / set_title_text(text) / set_back_target(id) / content() / add_focus(suffix, node, action, opts)
  / drop_focus(suffix) / focus_id(suffix) / back_control_id() / focus_controls()
  const SAFE_MARGIN := 8.0
PlaceholderScreen (extends ScreenContract)    register it for any id a later ticket has not replaced
UiStrings (extends RefCounted)               t(message_id, params) / has(message_id)
```

Freeze note as recorded in `ScreenRouter.gd`'s header: after UIR-03, screens register
themselves through `register()` and do not edit the router; only the integration owner
(UIR-22) or a coordinator-approved change does.

