# Integration wave 2 verification (2026-09-17, integrator)

Re-run, unmodified, in the isolated copy (engine `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`):

    $ "$GODOT" --headless --path godot/ --script res://tests/ui/router_audit.gd
    PASS 86/86
    exit=0                                    SCRIPT ERROR lines: 0
    # report literal scan scanned=12 files offenders=0 exemptions=1 whitelist=1

The count moved 11 -> 12 because `godot/src/ui/screens/MenuScreen.gd` (UIR-07) is the first
real screen in the lane and the scan reads it like every other file: **0 offenders**, no
whitelist entry needed. The router itself mounted it through `register("menu", …)` +
`go_to("menu")` in `screen_menu_audit.gd`, and the reachability audit is unchanged
(`PASS 21/21`). The `screen_changed`, payload and one-screen-at-a-time invariants were not
re-tested here beyond what UIR-07's audit asserts.
